# Android/IntelliJ
#
build/
# WHY `build/` above is not enough, and why the entries here are slashless: git's trailing-slash
# patterns match DIRECTORIES ONLY, so a build dir that is a SYMLINK (a local disk offload, e.g.
# build -> /extra/build/...) slips past it and `git add` takes it silently. That is how one got
# committed in #480; tracked, it dangles on any machine without that absolute path, and `mkdir`
# on a dangling symlink fails with "File exists" — so Gradle cannot create its own output dir and
# the build dies at `:app:generateAutolinkingNewArchitectureFiles`.
# `android/app/build` is covered at the end of this file; this is its sibling, same failure mode.
/android/build
.idea
.gradle
local.properties
*.iml
*.hprof
.cxx/
*.keystore
!debug.keystore
.kotlin/

# node.js
#
node_modules/
npm-debug.log
yarn-error.log

# fastlane
#
# It is recommended to not store the screenshots in the git repo. Instead, use fastlane to re-generate the
# screenshots whenever they are needed.
# For more information about the recommended setup visit:
# https://docs.fastlane.tools/best-practices/source-control/

**/fastlane/report.xml
**/fastlane/Preview.html
**/fastlane/screenshots
**/fastlane/test_output

